# Database SQL Basics – TryHackMe Lab

## 📌 Overview
This repository documents my hands-on learning and practical exercises from the Database SQL Basics room on TryHackMe.

The lab focuses on understanding relational databases, SQL syntax, and performing basic database operations through practical exercises.

## 🎯 Learning Objectives
- Understand database fundamentals.
- Learn the basics of SQL (Structured Query Language).
- Explore relational database structures.
- Understand tables, rows, and columns.
- Execute basic SQL queries.
- Retrieve and filter information from databases.

## 🛠️ Topics Covered

- Introduction to Databases
- Relational Database Management Systems (RDBMS)
- SQL Syntax and Commands
- SELECT Statements
- WHERE Clause
- INSERT Statements
- UPDATE Statements
- DELETE Statements
- ORDER BY Clause
- Basic Database Queries

## 💻 Practical Exercises

Performed hands-on SQL exercises to:
- Retrieve records from database tables.
- Filter data using conditions.
- Sort query results.
- Insert new records.
- Modify existing records.
- Understand basic database manipulation.

## 📸 Lab Screenshots

This repository includes screenshots of completed tasks and practical exercises to document my learning progress.

## 📚 Key Takeaways

Developed a foundational understanding of SQL queries, relational database concepts, and database operations. These skills are useful for cybersecurity, database management, and understanding how web applications interact with databases.

